WEBVTT
NOTE Fictional meeting for examples. Any resemblance to real people is coincidental.

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.000
<v Alex>Thanks for joining. Today we need to decide which vendor we go with for the Q4 launch.</v>

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.000
<v Jordan>Sounds good. I looked at both proposals over the weekend.</v>

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:01:10.000
<v Alex>Great. So quick recap. Vendor A is cheaper but needs six weeks to onboard. Vendor B costs about twenty percent more but can start in two weeks. Given the launch date, I think B is the safer option, but I want to hear what you both think. What worries you about B? And Sam, how does finance see the extra cost? Also do we need legal to review the contract first?</v>

4
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.000
<v Sam>Yeah.</v>

5
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:40.000
<v Jordan>My worry with B is their support hours. They only cover US time zones, and half our team is in Europe.</v>

6
00:01:41.000 --> 00:02:05.000
<v Alex>That's a fair point. Could we ask them for extended hours as part of the deal?</v>

7
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:30.000
<v Jordan>Probably. I can ask their account manager. I'll email her today and report back by Thursday.</v>

8
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:50.000
<v Alex>Perfect. Sam, on the budget side?</v>

9
00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:10.000
<v Sam>Let me check with finance. It might be fine.</v>

10
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:30.000
<v Alex>Okay, great. Let's assume B for now then.</v>

11
00:37:40.000 --> 00:38:00.000
<v Alex>Thanks everyone, talk soon.</v>
